       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum daily dose for adults of 3,200 mg/day (OTC labeling is lower, at 1,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and the extra dose adds no analgesic benefit.\n\nHere are some options within the labeled limits:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the maximum.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day) for mild to moderate pain.\n\nPossible typos include 1600 mg total per day (for example, 400 mg four times daily) or 800 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it. I can add a note such as \"take with food.\" If you need more than 3,200 mg/day for a particular indication, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy."
